# homeDX Platform Context

- Treat this repo as the full homeDX platform. The active app is `backend/` plus `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/`. `Cube APP V0.1.21/` is vendor/reference material. `mobile/` looks like an older/duplicate mobile tree, and `flutter/` is a local Flutter SDK checkout; avoid editing those unless the user explicitly targets them.
- Backend: NestJS 11 + TypeScript + Prisma/PostgreSQL. Entry points are `backend/src/main.ts` and `backend/src/app.module.ts`; it listens on `0.0.0.0:4000`. The Flutter-compatible REST API is `backend/src/controllers/mobile.controller.ts` under `/gg-homedx-json/gg-api/v1`.
- Backend domains include auth/users, rapid tests, Cube result submission, payments (Stripe/PayPal), licenses, test kits, certificates, audit logs, notifications, legal pages, and file uploads. Prisma models live in `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`.
- Mobile app: Flutter/Dart in `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/`, using Provider, GoRouter, `flutter_dotenv`, `shared_preferences`, HTTP REST, Bluetooth, Stripe, and PayPal WebView. App startup wires services/providers in `lib/main.dart`; routes are in `lib/config/app_router.dart`; app constants and API base URL are in `lib/utils/constants.dart`.
- Mobile API pattern: use `ApiService` for REST calls to `AppConstants.apiBaseUrl + AppConstants.apiPath` (`/gg-homedx-json/gg-api/v1`). Auth stores JWT in shared preferences and sends both `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and `x-auth-token` where applicable.
- Cube integration: Flutter `lib/services/cube_service.dart` talks to Android native `CubeBridge` in `android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/hdx_mobile/CubeAnalysisMethodChannel.kt` via MethodChannel `com.homedx.cube/analysis` and EventChannel `com.homedx.cube/events`. The native Cube SDK scans Cube devices, connects, evaluates on-device, reads measurement results, then Flutter submits normalized results to backend `submit-cube-data`.
- Cube pairing: if Android asks for a PIN/passkey, use the last six digits of the Cube serial number. The test flow is phone Bluetooth -> Cube SDK measurement -> Flutter reads results -> backend stores a `RapidTest` -> app displays results.
- WSL2 networking: backend should be reachable on port 4000. For a physical phone, set `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/.env` to `API_BASE_URL=http://<Windows-LAN-IP>:4000` using the Windows LAN IPv4, not the WSL IP. Re-run `setup-wsl-port-forward.cmd` as Admin after WSL restarts; `check-homedx-connectivity.ps1 -UpdateMobileEnv` can sync the mobile `.env`.
- Common commands: root `./deploy.sh all|backend|mobile`, `./stop.sh`; backend `npm run start:dev`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`; Flutter app `flutter pub get`, `flutter analyze`, `flutter test`, `flutter run`.
- **After Flutter/mobile UI changes:** rebuild and serve web so the user can verify (`fuser -k 8080/tcp; cd frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile && flutter run -d web-server --web-hostname 0.0.0.0 --web-port 8080 --release`). Ensure backend is up (`cd backend && npm run start:dev` on port 4000; matches `hdx_mobile/.env` `API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000`). On WSL2 + Windows browser, run `setup-wsl-port-forward.cmd` as Admin if API calls fail with "Failed to fetch".
- Testing expectations: backend has a Jest e2e smoke test at `backend/test/app.e2e-spec.ts`; Flutter has widget tests under `frontend/mobile/hdx_mobile/test/`. For Cube changes, manual E2E requires a real Android device and Cube: connect/pair, scan in-app, start a test, verify backend submission and displayed result.
